  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parasphaerichtys_lineatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>This is one of the smallest anabantoid fish in the world, hardly reaching 2 cm in length. Available size: 1–2 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parasphaerichtys_lineatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Origin: Burma (Myanmar).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parasphaerichtys_lineatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>In contrast to all other chocolate gouramis, it should be kept and bred in harder, slightly alkaline water (all other chocolate gouramis need soft, acidic water).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parasphaerichtys_lineatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Tankmates will not be harmed, provided they are also small and peaceful, for example Microdevario nana, Microrasbora spp. or Celestichthys spp. This is also true for conspecifics. Despite the small size of the fish, it is recommended to keep them in larger tanks and in groups, where all their fascinating behaviour can be observed.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parasphaerichtys_lineatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The sexes are hard to tell apart, except during the breeding season, when the male changes its coloration drastically and becomes bright orange-yellow.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parasphaerichtys_lineatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>In contrast to all other chocolate gouramis (which are mouthbrooders), this species is a bubble nest builder.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/parasphaerichtys_lineatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Parasphaerichthys: ancient Greek, meaning “similar to Sphaerichthys”, another genus of fish. lineatus: Latin, meaning “lined”, referring to the coloration.</p>"
    }
  ],
